327:- **Unplaced codec/crypto dependencies.** QOI 19/21, PNG 21–22, EVM 15/21/23 and Wasm 21 need endian byte operations; PNG also needs CRC32, EVM's full version needs Keccak (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)), and the HashMap at 23 behind the KV store, EVM 23 and the Wasm host tables needs a `hash` module, also unplaced (as are the optional `path` and text helpers). Their module arrivals are not placed, so these are scheduling gaps, not demonstrable later-slice conflicts. DEFLATE is an adopted PNG program requirement, not an independently scheduled std module. The crypto 7 stage is scalar only: arrays arrive at 15, so complete array-based ChaCha20/Poly1305/X25519 implementations cannot be claimed at 7 (slices 7 and 15 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices); the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)).
328:- **Wide-integer arithmetic is unplaced.** EVM 15 needs u256 arithmetic and X25519 and Poly1305 at 15/18 need arithmetic wider than u64 (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)); the integer types stop at 64 bits and no limb or wide-integer module is placed, so these stages have no module contract yet.
329:- **Proposed base64 at 17: legacy implementation conflicts.** This is not an adopted placement (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)). Legacy encode/decode allocate Bytes (`legacy/std/src/base64.con` line 40, `legacy/std/src/base64.con` line 62), before allocation at 19 and growable containers at 22; a fixed-buffer version has no decided API.
