docs/decisions.md:225:- **Q3.7** What is the raw-memory model and validity taxonomy? — Blocks with provenance; pointer = (prov: Option<BlockId>, addr: u64); integers carry no provenance; every access needs explicit validity premises. *Generalized 2026-11-08 by the [foundation decision](#foundation-q3): the address is read from a read-only target profile; the existing 64-bit little-endian profile is unchanged, and the provenance rules and the zero-byte exception are preserved.*
docs/decisions.md:296:- **P8** Server services under scripts/ — Keep only landing services: train, review, hook, landing bot. The status page, work queue, fuzz farm, perf tracking and nightly campaign all stop and are recorded as archived in RETENTION.tsv; each returns only with a roadmap task.
docs/decisions.md:302:- **P14** ci-3 handover: an exception to the archive requirement — Done by the owner on 2026-11-04: concrete-ci-3 was handed to stabileo; its fuzz corpus, perf history and leanprof data were not copied (an exception to the archive requirement).
